# Credentials. Match EVERY .env variant, not just the two we happened to think
# of — a `.env` line does not cover `.env.prod-backup`, `.env.dev`, etc.
# `.env.example` is the one intentional exception and is force-included below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
.DS_Store
coverage/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Internal audit artifacts (not for public consumption)
.audit/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live-validation artifacts (untracked 2026-08-16)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are records of real runs against a real tenant. They name live dataset,
# batch, TTL and work-order IDs, the sandbox, and the run UUIDs that tie them
# together. That is tenant metadata, and it was sitting in a public repository.
#
# They are still written locally and are still the audit trail — nothing about
# the ownership assertions or the cleanup guarantees changes. They just stop
# being published.
docs/run-ledgers/
scripts/emergency-cleanup-*.mjs
scripts/cleanup-phase*.mjs

# Synthetic payloads generated for ingestion tests, and captured live responses.
# Synthetic records are fabricated, but they are shaped like real profile data
# and are ingested into a real tenant; captures echo Adobe's request context.
*.ndjson
docs/live-captures/
.live-artifacts/
